# Walkthrough: Fix Perception Context Injection and Math Formatting

## 1. Problem Overview & Root Cause Analysis

### A. Camera Perception Context Hallucination
* **Root Cause**: In [websocket.py](file:///D:/AI%20ML%20Project/backend/app/api/websocket.py), the context injection block was evaluating `faces_count = len(latest_perception.get("faces", []))`. However, the detection pipeline in [detector.py](file:///D:/AI%20ML%20Project/backend/app/perception/detector.py) tracks people via YOLOv8 in the `"persons"` array and tracks gaze via `"gaze_x"` / `"gaze_y"`, leaving `"faces"` permanently empty (`[]`). Because `faces_count` was always `0`, `vc_str` evaluated unconditionally to `"No user visible currently."`, prompting the LLM to hallucinate: *"I don't see you in front of the camera."*

### B. Math Equations Rendering as Flat Text Without LaTeX
* **Root Cause 1 (Formatting Crash)**: In [engine.py](file:///D:/AI%20ML%20Project/backend/app/cognition/engine.py), calling `prompt_template.format(visual_context=visual_context)` failed with `ValueError: unexpected '{' in field name` because `SYSTEM_PROMPT_REASONING` contained LaTeX curly braces (e.g. `\frac{...}{...}`). This caused all reasoning candidates (Groq, Gemini, Nemotron) to crash during inference and drop into offline fallback.
* **Root Cause 2 (Delimiter Ingestion & Sanitization)**: Models like Groq frequently output LaTeX with `\[ ... \]` and `\( ... \)`. The frontend markdown parser ([App.jsx](file:///D:/AI%20ML%20Project/frontend/src/App.jsx)) uses `remark-math` and `rehype-katex`, which require standard `$` for inline math and `$$` for block math. Furthermore, sentence boundary splitting previously could split inside unclosed math expressions, fragmenting formulas.

